    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d684">

                <pb facs="0810" n="798" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg798"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00114 Pacific War/22: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Huddle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bern</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1942-02-24"
                            >February 24, 1942</date>.<lb/>[Received February 24—2:45
                        p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>732. American interests—Japan. Swiss Legation Tokyo telegraphs February 17 report
                    as follows in response to Department’s 86, January 13, paragraphs 1, 2, 3 and
                        3<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Japanese Government replies in substance ‘regarding paragraphs 1, 2, 3,
                            it has notified Intercroixrouge<anchor n="35" xml:id="d684-f1"/> of its
                            agreement exchange <pb facs="0811" n="799" xml:id="pg799"/> information
                            concerning prisoners and internees and also for establishment official
                            information bureau for prisoners of war’; as for paragraph 4 (3<hi
                                rendition="#italic">c</hi>) Japanese Foreign Office refers to note
                            communicated by my telegram January 30 (see Legation’s 398, February 4).
                            [”]</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huddle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d684-f1" n="35" xml:id="d684-f1-content">
                <p>International Committee of the Red Cross.</p>
            </note>
